From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wiaservc: event callback registration (3623)

wiaservc: event callback registration

RegisterEventCallbackInterface keeps the callback in a registration object
that unregisters itself when released; RegisterEventCallbackProgram/CLSID
write (or with WIA_UNREGISTER_EVENT_CALLBACK delete) the handler under
HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\StillImage\Events\<device>\<event>, so
only administrators can register. No event fires without a device. GetImageDlg
answers WIA_S_NO_DEVICE_AVAILABLE. The TWAIN/SANE path is untouched.
---
